                    briefing_r5_title: 'Round 5 — Pricing Night',
                    body_r1: '<strong>Prismview Analytics, Inc.</strong> — Boston B2B SaaS analytics. ARR $180M, 32% YoY, NRR 118%, Rule of 40 = 24, $84M cash, $95M venture debt. Confidential S-1 filed 60 days ago under JOBS Act EGC provisions; public 21 days. Filed range <strong>$18–$21</strong>, 22M primary shares, <strong>Morgan Stanley / Goldman / JPM</strong> on the cover. <em>AnalyticBridge broke issue last Thursday.</em> Two strategic buyers and Thoma Bravo have reverse-inquired at $2.4–2.8B. An informal SEC inquiry on revenue-recognition timing is open and undisclosed.<br><br>Select your peer group, price range, tranche structure, and gross spread.',
                    body_r2: 'The S-1 risk section goes under the lamp. Three defining calls: <strong>(1)</strong> the undisclosed SEC informal inquiry — <em>TSC v. Northway</em> and <em>Basic v. Levinson</em> materiality; <strong>(2)</strong> meme-stock volatility boilerplate; <strong>(3)</strong> MD&amp;A non-GAAP prominence under Reg G. Governance — dual-class, staggered board, forum-selection — sets the ISS / Glass Lewis signal that institutional voting desks will publish the week of pricing. Pre-announced Rule 10b5-1 plans manage the post-lockup trading story.',
                    body_r3: 'Day 7 of the road show. 38 one-on-ones, 4 group meetings. Preliminary demand: <strong>$18 → 62M</strong>, <strong>$19.50 → 44M</strong>, <strong>$21 → 22M</strong>, <strong>$22 → 12M</strong>. 68% long-only, 24% hedge fund, 8% retail. Fidelity, Capital Group, T. Rowe Price, and Wellington account for 28M of indicated demand. A Chicago PM grilled the team on Q3 NRR dropping to 114%; the exchange is leaking into the investor chat. <em>Quality of book matters more than coverage.</em> Decide on price talk, upsize, timeline, and anchor-signaling.',
                    body_r4: 'SEC Division of Corp Fin issues three comment rounds. Round A (14 items) is mechanical. <strong>Round B</strong> flags (i) ASC 606 SSP for the three flagged enterprise contracts, (ii) the undisclosed informal inquiry, (iii) customer concentration. <strong>Round C</strong> is material: staff asserts <em>$4.8M of Q3 revenue should have been ratable, not upfront.</em> A restatement delays the deal 45–60 days but produces a clean prospectus. Your responses will decide whether the S-1 clears, delays, or derails.',
                    body_r5: 'Pricing night. Final book: <strong>$22 → 3.1x covered, 72% LO</strong>; <strong>$24 → 1.9x, 58% LO</strong>; <strong>$25 → 1.3x, 41% LO</strong>. The CEO wants $24. The CFO is nervous about aftermarket trading. Two anchor LOs have indicated they will scale back above $23. Pricing math: at $22, net proceeds ~$452M, implied EV/ARR 16.0x, modeled +14–20% Day 1. Loughran-Ritter documents median IPO underpricing at ~15% — the <em>price of a clean deal</em>, not a bug. Price, allocate, set shoe strategy, and choose Day 1 posture.',
                    debrief_title: 'Deal Closed — Debrief',
                    debrief_body: 'The deal has priced. The leaderboard reflects the composite <em>Deal Quality Score</em> across Issuer Proceeds, Day 1 Performance, Allocation Quality, Disclosure Integrity, Syndicate Economics, Issuer-Bank Relationship, Governance Signal, and Regulatory Outcome. <br><br>Scroll the history table for the round-by-round ledger. The chart shows how each KPI evolved across the transaction.',
